## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates practical experience designing observable, scalable Azure telemetry pipelines with proper instrumentation, tenant isolation, and comprehensive monitoring integration for enterprise-grade media analytics platforms.

## Key Concepts

- OpenTelemetry integration across Event Hubs, Databricks, and Delta Lake
- End-to-end trace correlation and structured logging
- Adaptive sampling strategies and retention policies
- Tenant-level RBAC and data governance
- Comprehensive monitoring with Application Insights and Azure Monitor
- Real-time alerting and SLA management

## Code Example

```javascript
// Propagate correlation across services
const traceHeader = appInsights.getCorrelationContext();
const traceId = traceHeader.traceId;

// Instrument Event Hubs producer
eventHubProducer.send({
  body: eventData,
  properties: {
    traceId: traceId,
    tenantId: tenantId,
    region: region,
    timestamp: new Date().toISOString()
  }
});

// Configure OpenTelemetry sampling
const sampler = new ParentBasedSampler({
  root: new TraceIdRatioBasedSampler(0.01) // 1% production
});
```

## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates expertise in designing schema evolution and tenant isolation in Azure data pipelines while balancing flexibility with data integrity.

## Key Concepts

- Schema evolution and backward compatibility
- Per-tenant isolation in Delta Lake on ADLS Gen2
- Lightweight schema registry design
- Data quality gates and validation strategies
- Migration and rollback strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: validate and route incoming record by tenant/version
async function processRecord(record, tenantId) {
  const schema = await getSchema(tenantId);
  const validationResult = validateAgainstSchema(record, schema);
  if (!validationResult.valid) {
    await sendToDeadLetterQueue(record, validationResult.errors);
    return;
  }
  await writeToDeltaLake(record, tenantId, schema.version);
}
```

